The paper formalizes stochasticity **one-sided** — only the discrete score-function/REINFORCE estimator `∇θ E[log π(a|s)·Gₜ]` for division, and backprops pathwise only in the division-free cadherin model. The **code generalizes** this into a single trace/replay/`logp` contract that *also* admits reparameterized (pathwise) stochastic steps the paper never describes; the model picks the estimator per step via `pathwise = not scored`. Source wins.

